19
00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:02.020
Y2K. Maybe the most famous bug.

20
00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:05.820
Back in the sixties, memory was expensive.

21
00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.280
So programmers saved space:

22
00:03:08.280 --> 00:03:11.500
they stored the year with just two digits.

23
00:03:12.280 --> 00:03:14.660
1985? Became “85.”

24
00:03:14.940 --> 00:03:18.420
Then comes the year 2000: “double-zero.”

25
00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:21.420
And the computer reads it as… 1900.

26
00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:24.960
Born in ’85? Zero minus 85:

27
00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:27.460
